Lua 5.5.1 (released 24 Jul 2026), from https://www.lua.org/ftp/lua-5.5.1.tar.gz

The interpreter the command-line programs read their configuration files
with. Only the programs link it (bin/CMakeLists.txt); the library and pysif
never see it.

What is here is upstream's src/ directory, every file byte-for-byte as
released, less three that are not needed:

  Makefile         sif builds it with CMake
  lua.c, luac.c    the stand-alone interpreter and compiler

No file carries a local modification. Of what is here, only the core and the
libraries a configuration may use are compiled -- base, math, string, table,
utf8 and os, the last trimmed to a few read-only functions at run time; see
the list in bin/CMakeLists.txt.

LICENSE is the copyright notice from the end of lua.h, unchanged. It is MIT,
compatible with sif's GPL-3.0-or-later, and it ships in the wheel with the
other bundled libraries' licences.

To update: unpack the new release, replace every file here by its namesake
from src/ (leaving out the three above), refresh LICENSE from lua.h and the
version at the top of this file, and check the "Incompatibilities" section
of doc/manual.html against bin/sif-exodus/config.c.
